1
00:00:05,534 --> 00:00:07,764
What the heck are you dressed for?

2
00:00:08,534 --> 00:00:11,204
We're going to dig for sweet potatoes
at the kindergarten today!

3
00:00:11,204 --> 00:00:12,834
What did you see, and where did you see it?!

4
00:00:15,544 --> 00:00:16,144
According to the magazine at
the convenience store,

5
00:00:16,144 --> 00:00:17,314
The Future of Agriculture
According to the magazine at
the convenience store,

6
00:00:18,114 --> 00:00:22,104
everyone working at the farm is dressed like this.

7
00:00:22,914 --> 00:00:25,214
How do you expect to dig potatoes
with a bug catching net?!

8
00:00:33,634 --> 00:00:36,764
Kobato.

9
00:00:36,764 --> 00:00:39,604
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

10
00:00:39,604 --> 00:00:44,004
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

11
00:00:44,904 --> 00:00:48,214
Muzukashii na

12
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:50,984
Ureshii toki waratte

13
00:00:50,984 --> 00:00:55,284
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

14
00:00:55,854 --> 00:00:58,284
Na no ni

15
00:00:59,584 --> 00:01:03,954
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

16
00:01:04,394 --> 00:01:07,664
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

17
00:01:07,664 --> 00:01:11,154
Machikirenai yo

18
00:01:11,304 --> 00:01:17,074
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

19
00:01:17,074 --> 00:01:22,274
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

20
00:01:22,274 --> 00:01:25,114
Doko ni aru no?

21
00:01:25,114 --> 00:01:28,454
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

22
00:01:28,454 --> 00:01:31,284
Meippai kizu tsuite

23
00:01:31,284 --> 00:01:34,194
Seiippai hashitte

24
00:01:34,194 --> 00:01:38,164
Nan juu kai koronde naite

25
00:01:38,164 --> 00:01:41,194
Sore de mo mada

26
00:01:41,194 --> 00:01:45,224
Akireru kurai

27
00:01:45,704 --> 00:01:49,864
Ashita wo shinjiteru

28
00:01:59,684 --> 00:02:03,844
...Twilight Search.

29
00:02:07,854 --> 00:02:09,754
Thank you for your help again this year.

30
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:11,284
Oh it's my pleasure.

31
00:02:11,424 --> 00:02:13,764
Be my guest and take as many as you like.

32
00:02:14,164 --> 00:02:15,524
I can't thank you enough.

33
00:02:15,794 --> 00:02:19,234
Now listen. Whatever potatoes you
dig up, you carry yourself.

34
00:02:19,704 --> 00:02:22,364
Do not dig up more than you can carry.
Now, promise me that.

35
00:02:22,504 --> 00:02:25,374
Kobato, look! They're connected!

36
00:02:25,674 --> 00:02:27,374
Look how big this one is!

37
00:02:27,574 --> 00:02:31,374
You're right! This is like a treasure
hunt, don't you think?

38
00:02:33,214 --> 00:02:34,474
Ouch...

39
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:36,254
Wow...

40
00:02:36,254 --> 00:02:38,084
That one's huge!

41
00:02:38,184 --> 00:02:39,584
Wow!

42
00:02:41,094 --> 00:02:43,154
D-Dobato...!

43
00:02:43,824 --> 00:02:46,484
Kobato, your bum's all covered in dirt!

44
00:02:46,564 --> 00:02:47,684
Huh?

45
00:02:48,594 --> 00:02:50,064
Who could that be?

46
00:02:53,364 --> 00:02:57,274
He looks a bit older than the
children at Yomogi Kindergarten.

47
00:02:58,444 --> 00:03:00,564
Does he live here, I wonder?

48
00:03:00,814 --> 00:03:04,504
No. The grandchild living here is in high school.

49
00:03:04,844 --> 00:03:08,904
Well then where could he have come from?

50
00:03:16,824 --> 00:03:17,794
Hey you.

51
00:03:19,524 --> 00:03:20,624
Are you alone?

52
00:03:22,034 --> 00:03:23,624
Do you live near here?

53
00:03:29,734 --> 00:03:30,834
Hey wait!

54
00:03:49,994 --> 00:03:52,624
I'm sorry, I should have noticed earlier.

55
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:56,324
Oh well, some kids tend to be
up to no good, you know.

56
00:03:57,134 --> 00:03:59,264
I wonder if he's from around here.

57
00:04:01,034 --> 00:04:03,774
All right! Time to tidy up. We're leaving!

58
00:04:03,774 --> 00:04:05,604
Okay!

59
00:04:05,744 --> 00:04:07,574
Wow, we sure got a lot!

60
00:04:08,014 --> 00:04:09,744
Kobato!

61
00:04:10,384 --> 00:04:12,314
So many sweet potatoes!

62
00:04:13,244 --> 00:04:15,084
Look at all I got!

63
00:04:15,654 --> 00:04:16,514
Hey.

64
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:19,354
I thought I told you right at the beginning.

65
00:04:20,084 --> 00:04:22,144
You have to carry the potatoes
you dug up yourself.

66
00:04:25,494 --> 00:04:27,424
Okay, we're having baked sweet
potatoes when we get back.

67
00:04:27,594 --> 00:04:29,034
Yay!

68
00:04:29,634 --> 00:04:31,794
Kobato, are you going to be okay?

69
00:04:32,534 --> 00:04:34,234
Do you want me to help you?

70
00:04:39,004 --> 00:04:41,634
I'm fine! I can carry them all by myself!

71
00:04:41,974 --> 00:04:44,944
That's too many for you to carry. Let me help.

72
00:04:45,384 --> 00:04:49,544
No! It was a promise. We all carry
home what we dug up ourselves!

73
00:04:50,324 --> 00:04:51,914
Of course.

74
00:04:52,824 --> 00:04:55,224
He's so mean.

75
00:05:00,294 --> 00:05:04,134
Th-This is impossible! Give it up, Kobato!

76
00:05:07,004 --> 00:05:08,334
Young lady.

77
00:05:08,834 --> 00:05:09,904
I'll help you!

78
00:05:09,904 --> 00:05:11,634
Really?!

79
00:05:12,244 --> 00:05:13,804
Thank you very much.

80
00:05:18,644 --> 00:05:20,274
Are they ready yet?

81
00:05:20,554 --> 00:05:21,944
It's so smoky!

82
00:05:25,884 --> 00:05:27,284
Wow!

83
00:05:27,394 --> 00:05:28,684
Is it hot?

84
00:05:32,364 --> 00:05:33,324
Here you go!

85
00:05:33,594 --> 00:05:34,684
Thank you!

86
00:05:35,164 --> 00:05:37,354
Be careful, it's hot!

87
00:05:40,204 --> 00:05:41,324
Hey...

88
00:05:41,434 --> 00:05:42,524
Here you are.

89
00:05:44,544 --> 00:05:46,034
Delicious!

90
00:05:48,744 --> 00:05:50,544
So what do we do with all this?

91
00:05:51,544 --> 00:05:53,204
Shall we bake some more?

92
00:05:54,554 --> 00:05:56,644
Why don't we share it with the neighbors?

93
00:05:57,154 --> 00:05:59,084
People of 2-chome
Takahashi
Tsunomoto
Gokura
Shimada
People of 6-chome
Waki
Matsumoto
Ishino
Yoshihata

94
00:05:59,554 --> 00:06:03,924
Fujimoto, will you go with Kobato
and take them to those places?

95
00:06:04,424 --> 00:06:07,824
I'll go alone. It'll be faster.

96
00:06:08,734 --> 00:06:11,194
Hmm... But I'd prefer you both go.

97
00:06:12,604 --> 00:06:16,294
It would be a good opportunity for Kobato
to get to know the neighbors too.

98
00:06:16,474 --> 00:06:17,994
Do you mind, Kobato?

99
00:06:18,504 --> 00:06:19,604
My pleasure!

100
00:06:23,014 --> 00:06:25,444
Kobato is ready!

101
00:06:26,314 --> 00:06:27,804
I won't tell you to help.

102
00:06:28,514 --> 00:06:29,744
Just stay out of my way.

103
00:06:34,494 --> 00:06:36,254
My sweet potatoes!

104
00:06:36,424 --> 00:06:40,794
He's just too mean. All he says to
me is to not get in the way.

105
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:44,254
But he didn't tell you not to tag along.

106
00:06:45,804 --> 00:06:50,434
But he took the potatoes from me.
I was going to hand them out.

107
00:06:51,044 --> 00:06:55,034
You could also say that he's carrying
them for you because they're heavy.

108
00:07:02,584 --> 00:07:03,774
Yes?

109
00:07:04,824 --> 00:07:06,614
We've come from Yomogi Kindergarten.

110
00:07:06,854 --> 00:07:11,024
We went digging for sweet potatoes and thought
you might like some. They're very good!

111
00:07:11,564 --> 00:07:14,324
Well... Thank you.

112
00:07:18,834 --> 00:07:20,494
We're from Yomogi Kindergarten!

113
00:07:20,604 --> 00:07:22,694
Oh, thank you.

114
00:07:24,344 --> 00:07:25,534
Have some sweet potatoes!

115
00:07:25,774 --> 00:07:26,944
Thank you.

116
00:07:26,944 --> 00:07:28,704
We're from Yomogi Kindergarten!

117
00:07:31,244 --> 00:07:32,714
Fujimoto!

118
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:34,404
Huh?

119
00:07:34,614 --> 00:07:37,954
We're almost finished handing
out all of the sweet potatoes!

120
00:07:38,754 --> 00:07:40,014
Yeah.

121
00:07:42,354 --> 00:07:43,554
Hey!

122
00:07:48,094 --> 00:07:49,324
Well, well.

123
00:07:51,934 --> 00:07:53,234
You're home.

124
00:07:53,534 --> 00:07:54,794
Good afternoon!

125
00:07:55,274 --> 00:07:56,294
Oh my.

126
00:07:56,704 --> 00:07:59,174
Young lady. How nice to see you.

127
00:07:59,674 --> 00:08:00,834
Yes!

128
00:08:00,974 --> 00:08:03,374
Have you been well, Milk?

129
00:08:05,244 --> 00:08:07,544
You've grown a little, haven't you?

130
00:08:07,914 --> 00:08:09,284
Yes, she has.

131
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:11,554
She's quite healthy.

132
00:08:17,264 --> 00:08:18,384
It's him.

133
00:08:18,624 --> 00:08:21,064
Oh. He was just passing by.

134
00:08:21,064 --> 00:08:22,654
Asked me if he could use the faucet.

135
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:24,854
Said he'd been out digging potatoes.

136
00:08:25,834 --> 00:08:26,904
Hey you!

137
00:08:26,904 --> 00:08:28,304
You were at the...

138
00:08:28,434 --> 00:08:29,404
Take this!

139
00:08:29,534 --> 00:08:30,594
Wait!

140
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:38,104
I told you to wait, didn't I?!

141
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:39,734
Let go, you thief!

142
00:08:42,154 --> 00:08:45,414
Those are my words, you potato thief!

143
00:08:45,954 --> 00:08:47,754
Let me down!

144
00:08:48,354 --> 00:08:51,194
Fujimoto, what are you doing?!

145
00:08:51,624 --> 00:08:53,864
I'm taking this thief to the police.

146
00:08:53,864 --> 00:08:57,664
No! Please don't! I'll give them back.
I'll give them back, really!

147
00:09:01,534 --> 00:09:03,094
Just as I thought.

148
00:09:03,734 --> 00:09:05,034
You've run away from home.

149
00:09:05,244 --> 00:09:06,574
Run away from home?!

150
00:09:26,924 --> 00:09:28,154
What's your name?

151
00:09:31,634 --> 00:09:33,264
So now you're not talking?

152
00:09:39,604 --> 00:09:40,914
What's your name?

153
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,634
Potato Thief will do.

154
00:09:43,074 --> 00:09:44,564
I'm not a potato thief!

155
00:09:45,984 --> 00:09:47,184
Of course.

156
00:09:47,184 --> 00:09:49,014
You do have a proper name, don't you?

157
00:09:55,024 --> 00:09:56,084
Keita...

158
00:09:58,094 --> 00:10:01,464
Keita? Why did you leave home?

159
00:10:02,764 --> 00:10:05,354
I wanted to go to my old house.

160
00:10:05,704 --> 00:10:07,764
Your old... house?

161
00:10:08,474 --> 00:10:13,774
It's where I used to live. My mom switched
companies, so we had to move.

162
00:10:14,814 --> 00:10:17,434
So how was it? Your old house.

163
00:10:20,854 --> 00:10:22,814
I haven't been there yet.

164
00:10:25,184 --> 00:10:27,484
Are you on your way there now?

165
00:10:28,224 --> 00:10:30,414
I was going to go, but...

166
00:10:30,764 --> 00:10:32,664
You forget where it was, don't you?

167
00:10:33,494 --> 00:10:34,894
I haven't forgotten!

168
00:10:35,594 --> 00:10:38,304
No, the look on your face tells me you forgot.

169
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:39,664
No!

170
00:10:40,204 --> 00:10:42,764
You wouldn't forget your own house, would you?

171
00:10:43,804 --> 00:10:45,034
Well...

172
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:48,044
I was only in kindergarten when we moved, so...

173
00:10:48,544 --> 00:10:50,514
Maybe I kind of got lost...

174
00:10:50,814 --> 00:10:53,244
That's called "forgetting".

175
00:10:53,244 --> 00:10:54,774
I haven't forgotten!

176
00:10:57,954 --> 00:10:59,114
Keita.

177
00:10:59,254 --> 00:11:03,624
If you tell us what your house looked like,
we might be able to help you find it.

178
00:11:04,194 --> 00:11:06,184
Can you draw a picture of the house?

179
00:11:07,394 --> 00:11:09,024
Yeah! I can do that!

180
00:11:10,634 --> 00:11:21,404
Um... it was... it had a red roof, and windows
here and here, an antenna, and also...

181
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:26,844
Draw what was around the house too, okay?
That will make it easier to find.

182
00:11:27,654 --> 00:11:33,414
Oh right. There was a mailbox here.
And a dog lived next door.

183
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:40,054
That's a big dog.

184
00:11:40,464 --> 00:11:42,824
He always barked when I went by.

185
00:11:50,474 --> 00:11:53,404
Grade 2
Name: Keita Yoshimura

186
00:11:57,014 --> 00:11:58,604
And you know what else?

187
00:11:58,944 --> 00:12:01,884
My mom always baked cookies and stuff.

188
00:12:02,914 --> 00:12:04,214
Wow!

189
00:12:14,034 --> 00:12:20,664
She read me books and took me camping
and to the amusement park on holidays.

190
00:12:23,304 --> 00:12:24,434
Keita?

191
00:12:26,444 --> 00:12:28,964
I want to go back to my old house!

192
00:12:35,414 --> 00:12:36,684
Fujimoto.

193
00:12:38,054 --> 00:12:41,994
I'd like to help Keita find his house.

194
00:12:51,304 --> 00:12:55,134
We've only got a dog and a mailbox to go by.
That's not going to find us his house.

195
00:12:56,934 --> 00:12:58,994
Isn't there anything else you can remember?

196
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:15,884
Which way? Right? Left?

197
00:13:17,154 --> 00:13:19,594
Um... Th-This way.

198
00:13:20,494 --> 00:13:22,084
No this way?

199
00:13:39,584 --> 00:13:41,344
Oh! I know this place!

200
00:13:41,714 --> 00:13:43,084
I've been here before.

201
00:13:43,714 --> 00:13:46,244
Is that right? We might be close then.

202
00:13:46,654 --> 00:13:48,984
That's wonderful, isn't it Keita?

203
00:13:49,194 --> 00:13:50,214
Yeah.

204
00:14:05,044 --> 00:14:06,474
Did you want to get a drink?

205
00:14:07,374 --> 00:14:10,404
But that's okay. I need to conserve.

206
00:14:10,884 --> 00:14:12,214
Conserve?

207
00:14:12,844 --> 00:14:15,684
You know some difficult words.

208
00:14:16,954 --> 00:14:19,114
My mom always says that.

209
00:14:19,354 --> 00:14:20,514
Over here.

210
00:14:20,654 --> 00:14:22,184
Fujimoto?

211
00:14:26,394 --> 00:14:27,164
Please help yourself.

212
00:14:27,164 --> 00:14:28,534
Please help yourself.
Why those are...

213
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:29,124
Please help yourself.

214
00:14:29,934 --> 00:14:32,694
Pears. Can't you tell?

215
00:14:32,934 --> 00:14:33,904
Here.

216
00:14:35,904 --> 00:14:37,134
Is it okay?

217
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:39,204
Let's leave some of these in return.

218
00:14:44,284 --> 00:14:45,904
Mmm, this is good!

219
00:14:48,354 --> 00:14:49,644
It is good.

220
00:14:51,354 --> 00:14:53,374
Fujimoto can be a pretty good guy.

221
00:14:53,654 --> 00:14:57,114
Well, I should hope so.

222
00:14:57,524 --> 00:14:59,114
Give me some of that pear, too.

223
00:15:04,564 --> 00:15:05,554
This is great!

224
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:14,404
Could this dog be?

225
00:15:17,914 --> 00:15:19,544
Which means...

226
00:15:20,544 --> 00:15:22,274
Next door...

227
00:15:35,994 --> 00:15:38,194
This isn't my house.

228
00:15:38,734 --> 00:15:43,534
Yoshimura

229
00:15:46,944 --> 00:15:47,904
We're going in.

230
00:15:58,154 --> 00:16:00,714
Yoshimura

231
00:16:10,464 --> 00:16:11,454
Stay back.

232
00:16:15,434 --> 00:16:16,834
My room...

233
00:16:19,104 --> 00:16:21,164
It seems to be locked.

234
00:16:22,414 --> 00:16:23,904
We have no choice but to break it.

235
00:16:24,314 --> 00:16:25,374
No!
Fujimoto!

236
00:16:26,314 --> 00:16:27,544
P-Please...

237
00:16:29,854 --> 00:16:31,474
Please don't break it.

238
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:42,254
You don't want to go home
to where you live now?

239
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:46,464
Because Grandpa's there.

240
00:16:47,904 --> 00:16:49,334
Grandpa?

241
00:16:49,634 --> 00:16:50,794
Yeah.

242
00:16:51,204 --> 00:16:55,194
My mom and I, we live at
my grandpa's house now.

243
00:16:55,714 --> 00:16:59,544
Keita, you don't like your grandpa?

244
00:17:00,114 --> 00:17:02,344
He's not nice. He's always mean to me.

245
00:17:03,254 --> 00:17:04,774
Always mean?

246
00:17:08,024 --> 00:17:09,144
Well...

247
00:17:10,724 --> 00:17:13,354
Every morning he nags at me to get up.

248
00:17:15,834 --> 00:17:18,294
Hey! Keita! Get out of bed already!

249
00:17:18,934 --> 00:17:20,564
Hurry up and put that away!

250
00:17:22,334 --> 00:17:26,534
I want to watch more TV at night
and play computer games, too.

251
00:17:28,514 --> 00:17:29,474
Keita!

252
00:17:29,474 --> 00:17:31,514
Grandpa, what did you do that for?!

253
00:17:31,514 --> 00:17:33,914
You shouldn't be up so late. Get to bed!

254
00:17:35,184 --> 00:17:39,174
And at dinner time, he's always
telling me to eat stuff I don't like.

255
00:17:39,524 --> 00:17:41,144
Stuff you don't like?

256
00:17:41,454 --> 00:17:43,944
Like small fish and vegetables...

257
00:17:45,364 --> 00:17:46,584
Keita!

258
00:17:46,894 --> 00:17:48,794
I will not have you wasting food!

259
00:17:48,994 --> 00:17:50,724
Eat what you are served!

260
00:17:51,464 --> 00:17:54,204
Do you think that's being mean?

261
00:17:54,204 --> 00:17:57,004
Sure! Grandpa hates me!

262
00:17:57,274 --> 00:17:59,794
That's why he's always scolding me like that!

263
00:17:59,874 --> 00:18:04,244
He wants me to leave! So I
decided to leave that home!

264
00:18:05,214 --> 00:18:06,614
Keita...

265
00:18:07,284 --> 00:18:10,484
Ms. Sayaka is always telling the
kindergarten students to eat

266
00:18:10,484 --> 00:18:14,884
small fish and vegetables because
they're full of nutrition.

267
00:18:16,024 --> 00:18:17,694
Who's Ms. Sayaka?

268
00:18:17,694 --> 00:18:22,464
Ms. Sayaka is very kind and loves
the children very much.

269
00:18:22,694 --> 00:18:24,824
She's a teacher at Yomogi Kindergarten.

270
00:18:25,934 --> 00:18:27,494
Kind?

271
00:18:40,714 --> 00:18:41,974
Keita!

272
00:18:46,424 --> 00:18:49,354
If you're finished taking
your bath, get to bed!

273
00:18:56,194 --> 00:19:01,154
It's difficult to tell the difference between
someone being mean and not being mean.

274
00:19:01,574 --> 00:19:05,164
But if you look real carefully,
you might be able to tell.

275
00:19:06,204 --> 00:19:11,164
Keita, were you planning on
baking sweet potatoes here?

276
00:19:12,014 --> 00:19:16,474
We baked sweet potatoes together
before and they tasted good.

277
00:19:18,984 --> 00:19:21,684
You take responsibility and take
some of these home with you.

278
00:19:21,824 --> 00:19:22,844
Huh?

279
00:19:23,224 --> 00:19:25,624
I apologized to the lady at the farm for you.

280
00:19:26,494 --> 00:19:30,194
She dug up too many and
this is incredibly heavy.

281
00:19:30,764 --> 00:19:32,754
Isn't that nice, Keita?

282
00:19:36,704 --> 00:19:37,934
Yes.

283
00:19:46,444 --> 00:19:48,614
Can you really get home all by yourself?

284
00:19:48,614 --> 00:19:50,314
Not a problem!

285
00:19:50,384 --> 00:19:52,014
Keita?!

286
00:19:53,224 --> 00:19:54,954
Keita!

287
00:20:00,764 --> 00:20:02,024
Grandpa...

288
00:20:04,864 --> 00:20:06,024
Go on.

289
00:20:11,604 --> 00:20:13,264
Grandpa!

290
00:20:21,814 --> 00:20:22,944
Keita!

291
00:20:23,914 --> 00:20:25,854
Grandpa!

292
00:20:27,054 --> 00:20:28,544
Keita!

293
00:20:33,464 --> 00:20:34,394
Keita!

294
00:20:34,394 --> 00:20:35,384
Ouch!

295
00:20:36,764 --> 00:20:39,924
Oww! What are you doing, you old fart?

296
00:20:40,564 --> 00:20:43,474
Don't you worry me like that, you silly fool!

297
00:20:44,704 --> 00:20:46,134
Come! We're going home!

298
00:20:48,844 --> 00:20:50,204
Okay.

299
00:20:54,244 --> 00:20:56,144
You're mom's waiting for you at home.

300
00:20:56,654 --> 00:20:57,614
Okay.

301
00:21:00,054 --> 00:21:03,824
Keita is just about to get on the
train with his grandfather.

302
00:21:04,494 --> 00:21:06,484
Oh not at all. Well then.

303
00:21:07,964 --> 00:21:12,094
Fujimoto, you knew Keita's
home phone number?

304
00:21:12,264 --> 00:21:15,234
Was it you that called Keita's grandfather over?

305
00:21:15,234 --> 00:21:18,434
I don't know. Say, I'm hungry.

306
00:21:19,004 --> 00:21:20,304
Huh?

307
00:21:22,044 --> 00:21:24,104
You want to go home and steam
some sweet potatoes?

308
00:21:24,174 --> 00:21:26,574
Um... Yes.

309
00:21:26,844 --> 00:21:28,334
What is it?

310
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,044
Uh, nothing.

311
00:21:32,154 --> 00:21:33,354
Good evening.

312
00:21:33,354 --> 00:21:33,954
Hi.

313
00:21:33,954 --> 00:21:35,324
Domoto.
Hi.

314
00:21:36,224 --> 00:21:37,524
On your way home?

315
00:21:37,524 --> 00:21:39,824
I've got stuff to do. I'm going on ahead.

316
00:21:39,824 --> 00:21:41,094
Huh?

317
00:21:41,294 --> 00:21:42,424
Stuff to do?

318
00:21:42,794 --> 00:21:45,464
We went digging for sweet potatoes
with the kindergarten today

319
00:21:46,034 --> 00:21:48,224
and went around handing out
potatoes to the neighbors.

320
00:21:48,374 --> 00:21:49,534
I see.

321
00:21:49,534 --> 00:21:51,234
Fujimoto, he's...

322
00:21:53,874 --> 00:21:56,204
He's actually a nice person isn't he?

323
00:21:58,644 --> 00:22:02,844
Mhm, Fujimoto's a good guy.

324
00:22:07,854 --> 00:22:10,154
Ah, this one's from that rascal.

325
00:22:10,824 --> 00:22:14,664
Keita looked very sad when he
saw the old house though.

326
00:22:15,034 --> 00:22:18,984
I suppose this kompeito is because he
understood how his grandfather truly feels.

327
00:22:21,234 --> 00:22:22,664
I guess so.

328
00:22:23,404 --> 00:22:26,634
Well now for today's score... Seeing that
Fujimoto did much of the work...

329
00:22:27,104 --> 00:22:28,704
You get half, fifty points!

330
00:22:29,174 --> 00:22:33,584
Huh? But Fujimoto was mean
to me this morning.

331
00:22:34,244 --> 00:22:38,614
You're right. Then that offsets the
points and Fujimoto gets a zero.

332
00:22:39,224 --> 00:22:41,744
And you get seventy points
because you tried hard.

333
00:22:42,024 --> 00:22:45,424
Would you mind erasing first before re-writing?

334
00:22:45,424 --> 00:22:49,454
You complain too much. For that,
you're back down to fifty!

335
00:22:49,694 --> 00:22:51,164
Erase it properly, first...

336
00:22:51,164 --> 00:22:52,864
Oh, shut up! Twenty-five points!

337
00:22:52,864 --> 00:22:54,064
What?!

338
00:22:54,064 --> 00:22:57,004
Do you still have a problem? Then 12.5 points!

339
00:22:57,004 --> 00:23:00,334
Oh! My face is all covered in ink now!

340
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

341
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

342
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

343
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

344
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Jibun no kage wo

345
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

346
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
Sore nara

347
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

348
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

349
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

350
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

351
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
Shinpai nante iranai yo

352
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Issho ni iru kara

353
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

354
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:26,124
Fushigi da

355
00:24:26,124 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...Hidden Prayer.
Fushigi da

356
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,754
Next episode
...Hidden Prayer.

